    "accepted_contract": "Complete classification of the 81 rank-two and 431 rank-three residually connected firm flag-transitive coset geometries for M22 with maximal object stabilizers, up to the specified group-automorphism equivalence, together with a corrected canonical table and explicit dispositions of all 431 physical source rows.",
    "findings": [
      "Read the complete six-page mathematical exposition and all named proof arguments. Coset realization, exclusion of repeated maximal stabilizers, generation criterion for connected residues, finite completion-orbit criterion and exhaustive pair-to-triple augmentation supply the written proof architecture. The cardinality argument uses finite groups, as in this M22 application; a future detached common theorem must state this restriction explicitly.",
      "Read the census, validation and coordinate programs, and the literal-configuration/reconciliation interfaces. Fresh author traversal starts from the classical subgroup catalogue and actual permutation group, not the 431 historical geometry rows: 156 subgroup conjugacy classes, eight maximal classes, 2300 maximal subgroups, 81 pair classes, 11866 augmented triples,1193 accepted before fusion and431 final classes.",
      "Distinct root GAP program checks the actual group witnesses, maximal-stabilizer membership,81 pairs,431 triples, all1293 residue generations and panels. It compares actual completion orbit sets, not only their cardinalities. It does not import an author program. Root did not write a second exhaustive census traversal; completeness also relies on the reviewed generic enumeration proof and fresh author traversal.",
      "Root separately reconstructed all35 two-dimensional subspaces of the four-dimensional binary quotient of the rank14 orthogonal space by the rank10 literal seed. Exactly four4096-word codes have the required weights; each yields759 octads covering all42504 five-subsets exactly once. The four full labelled block sets agree with the frozen output. No presumed QR relabelling was used.",
      "Root independently reextracted all431 physical primary table rows from the bound PDF, preserving labels, printed numbers and Borel notation. The duplicate printed61 and absent62 do not alter the431 physical-row count. Root also reconstructed all endecad-complement closures and every candidate set for all three explicit readings, preserving undefined configurations.",
      "The source2010 definition allows each endecad complement independently. The older2003 canonical infinity extension is a separate diagnostic convention. The primary reading yields415 compatible rows representing413 distinct classes and16 incompatible rows; the canonical reading gives412 and410; the literal-object reading gives401 and400,29 incompatible and one undefined row. These are exact row-mapping diagnostics, not alternative census cardinalities.",
      "Read and visually checked the needed predecessor MOG, seed and refined-pair conventions. The displayed M56(0_2) objects and printed pair order disagree; M88(5_1) has an object which is not an endecad; e4 is not defined literally. The provisional fourth-endecad reading stays labelled. The three colon configurations are tested in all four compatible codes: two fail completion transitivity despite local generation; one belongs to census class338.",
      "Borel group names are matched to actual small-group data. Juxtaposed p^aH notation means the stated elementary-abelian normal kernel and quotient, without assuming an unspecified action or splitting. Historical unavailable geo[] identities are not invented. The 48-page predecessor is retained notation evidence, not another recovered original.",
      "Fresh author replay checks65 frozen exports, the two bound primary editions and11 historical pins, passes15 genuine omission/mutation controls and renders all36 new pages with matching page text and all seven whole mathematical programs included. Six known GAP unbound-global syntax warnings in the census/validator are recorded in the author report; the distinct GAP check has no stderr.",
      "Classical identification of M22, completeness of TomLib, group algorithms, and classical Steiner/Golay correspondences remain explicit retained facts. This review is written and computational, with zero Lean declarations. No full formal proof, historical priority, new conjecture solution, numerical compression factor or public source-count increment is asserted."
